{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources","id":1024148,"title":"Status and Resources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-30T01:07:22-08:00","id":1024148,"title":"Status and Resources","content":"First of all, sorry if this topic has been discussed before. I have searched on the forums for some similar topic under the keywords &quot;resources status&quot; and have found nothing.<br /> <br /> Now, to the question I have: doest the Status merit, depending on the group you have status, give a salary, or it has to be reflected by the resources Merit?<br /> <br /> The CoD book says, on Status<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, she has access to group facilities, resources, and funding. Depending on the group, this could be limited by red tape and requisitioning processes. It\u2019s also dependent on the resources the particular group has available. </div> </div> </div>But it says nothing on salary.<br /> <br /> Also, the CoD book says, on Resources,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She might live in an upscale condo, but if her income is tied up in the mortgage and child support payments, she might have little money to throw around </div> </div> </div>Also, the money has to come from somewhere.<br /> <br /> I find this incoherent. Imagine the following situation: <br /> <br /> I imagine a dialog between narrator and player like this: <br /> - N: Ok, you got Resources 5. Where this money comes from?<br /> - P: I am the president of a multinational, a Bruce Wayne type.<br /> - N: Ok, but you have to buy Status 5 on the Company.<br /> - P: I have no points left! Mmmm... then I buy Status 5 (CEO of the company) instead of resources 5.<br /> - N: Ok, but if you drop Resources to 0 you would not be able to portrait that &quot;Bruce Wayne&quot; character you want.<br /> - P: What? But he is the CEO, he has to have a big salary! <br /> - N: Sorry, Resources 0 is Resources 0. This means your CEO expends all his salary, you will have to tell how this happens. <br /> - P: Then I keep Resources 5.<br /> - N: Ok, where this money comes from?<br /> - P: I am a CEO.<br /> - N: Nope, if you want to have influence in a company, you have to buy Status 5.<br /> - P: So, you are telling me that I have to spend all my 10 points on Status 5 and Resources 5?<br /> - N: Yep.<br /> <br /> Ok, this is a extreme situation for an example, but what happens when a player wants to portrait a police, detective, doctor, gang leader... people with influence, and to reflect that influence they send points on making the detective a better detective, giving allies and contacts to the gang leader... and... Resource 0, really?<br /> <br /> How would you manage it?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:03:10-08:00","id":1024160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources#post1024148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you manage it?</div> </div> </div> </div>By not trying to start with a concept that requires Resources 5 + Status 5, just like I wouldn't start with a concept that requires multiple maxed-out Disciplines or 10 in a power stat.<br /> <br /> Edit: To elaborate, there's no requirement for the CEO of a company to have Status 5 within it. Maybe he's new, maybe he's not very good at his job, or maybe he's just a total recluse. Vampire touches on this a bit with the example of a Sheriff having more Status than the Prince of the City, but trying to force a Status 5 requirement for being in the 'top' position is really boxed-in thinking.<br /> <br /> There's also no requirement for Resources 5 to come from a job that would naturally lead to status, anyway. Trust fund kids, lucky investors, etc all exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 12-30-2016, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:27:04-08:00","id":1024167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources#post1024148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, to the question I have: doest the Status merit, depending on the group you have status, give a salary, or it has to be reflected by the resources Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Status does not inherently grant you a salary or the Resources Merit, because Status is used to represent any number of different types of organizations. Not all of them are going to follow the corporate structure where the more authority you have in the organization the more likely you are to pull significant (or any) money from it, and some situations where that would be &quot;normal&quot; might not even apply.<br /> <br /> For example,a character could be a lawyer and the son of the president of a hospital, and said lawyer does pro bono work for the hospital. The combination of his parent's clout and the respect earned by his volunteer work would be measured by the Status Merit, even while he explicitly draws no money from this and it would be at best (due to tax right offs) tangentially related to his Resource rating.<br /> <br /> As well, as you note, having a salary does not equate to a Resources rating. Your Resources represent your extra cash after you've covered your needs and obligations.<br /> <br /> If a character is the CEO of a company and thus has Status 5, but doesn't take any dots in Resources, it means that character's current financial obligations - regardless of how many zeros are attached to that job title's salary - don't leave any cash left over to be enjoying the wealth such a position is associated with.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that while Resources is very useful, mechanically there's nothing you can get with Resources that you can't get by other means; it'll just be slower and have more consequences. A high Status low/no Resources character can use their Status to all sorts of effect, but unlike Resources it will face scrutiny. A CEO that uses their Status to use company money to pay of various expenses that gets too sloppy with justifying them as related to the business (or just does it too often for too much) has a board to answer to, or an IRS audit to look forward to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find this incoherent. </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to explain this. What is incoherent here? Status is your position with an organization. Resources is how much spending cash you have available to you. The only possible incoherence you've demonstrated is introduced by your hypothetical player's expectations, not the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, this is a extreme situation for an example, but what happens when a player wants to portrait a police, detective, doctor, gang leader... people with influence, and to reflect that influence they send points on making the detective a better detective, giving allies and contacts to the gang leader... and... Resource 0, really? </div> </div> </div>Part of the rules of the game are to set an even starting point for player characters. This inherently means certain concepts are not appropriate as baseline 0 XP starting level characters. If you can't make what you want with the dots available, the options you have are to cut back on your character a bit, or talk to your ST about running a game with starting XP so you can have more stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would you manage it? </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure what the problem is beyond, &quot;I might not have enough points to make my character!&quot; which isn't a matter of Status and Resources in particular. And I handle that issue by working with my players that have this issue (usually ones not used to point-buy systems) to try to figure out a pared down version of the concept that they can make with the available dots/starting XP or find a different concept they'd enjoy that doesn't have this issue if that can't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:55:38-08:00","id":1024176,"title":"","content":"So, I understand then that:<br /> <br /> Status = Influence, NOT hierarchy<br /> Resources = extra cash left. NOT salary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1024167#post1024167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have to explain this. What is incoherent here? Status is your position with an organization. Resources is how much spending cash you have available to you. The only possible incoherence you've demonstrated is introduced by your hypothetical player's expectations, not the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said it is incoherent because I associated and understood the Status merit with a position in the hierarchy aof an organization, and not as an Influence indicator. Your explanations has helped to understand this a lot.<br /> <br /> So, correct me if I am wrng with the following examples:<br /> <br /> The favourite waitress of a gang leader could have Status 4 on the gang, not because she is on top of the gang, but because she has influence on the opinions of the gang leader, and no one wants to have problems with her. Also, she's so nice and charmfull that everybody in the gang has the &quot;no mess with Betty&quot; sentence programmed in their brains.<br /> <br /> The mentioned CEO could have a Mansion, 5 expensive cars, butlers and maids, and a private jet... but resources 0 because all the money goes to maintain his style of life, right?<br /> <br /> Or he could have Resources 5 but Status 1 on the company because, although been the CEO, he is tied to the decisions of the shareholders or the real owner of the company, and is so closely looked with a magnifier lens that he cannot go to the toilet without filling a form.<br /> <br /> A boy with Status (Memorial Hospital) 2 could be a loved volunteer in the urgecies of that Hospital, so much that when he needs help, he got it from the staff of the urgencies (nurses, doctors,cleaners...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1024167#post1024167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the rules of the game are to set an even starting point for player characters. This inherently means certain concepts are not appropriate as baseline 0 XP starting level characters. If you can't make what you want with the dots available, the options you have are to cut back on your character a bit, or talk to your ST about running a game with starting XP so you can have more stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot this part. Thanks<br /> <br /> As you say, I will handle this with the players to explain better the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:14:21-08:00","id":1024215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1024176#post1024176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I understand then that:<br /> <br /> Status = Influence, NOT hierarchy<br /> Resources = extra cash left. NOT salary.<br /> <br /> So, correct me if I am wrng with the following examples:<br /> <br /> The favourite waitress of a gang leader could have Status 4 on the gang, not because she is on top of the gang, but because she has influence on the opinions of the gang leader, and no one wants to have problems with her. Also, she's so nice and charmfull that everybody in the gang has the &quot;no mess with Betty&quot; sentence programmed in their brains.<br /> <br /> The mentioned CEO could have a Mansion, 5 expensive cars, butlers and maids, and a private jet... but resources 0 because all the money goes to maintain his style of life, right?<br /> <br /> Or he could have Resources 5 but Status 1 on the company because, although been the CEO, he is tied to the decisions of the shareholders or the real owner of the company, and is so closely looked with a magnifier lens that he cannot go to the toilet without filling a form.<br /> <br /> A boy with Status (Memorial Hospital) 2 could be a loved volunteer in the urgecies of that Hospital, so much that when he needs help, he got it from the staff of the urgencies (nurses, doctors,cleaners...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no need for correction. They're all good examples of Status-Resources imbalance (&quot;imbalance&quot; for lack of a better word)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:47:08-08:00","id":1024228,"title":"","content":"Also one more thing to look over Status understanding - even in supernatural societies it's more 'you are having large influance on our faction', than direct level of hierarchy. In <b>Mage</b> Order books, various titles have needed Status levels, but then are accompanied by statement that 'those levels are for average representatives - character can have higher or lower Status in Order, but will have repercussions. Lower Status than needed will be not take seriously on they positions and those higher will have unexpected influance on running of organisations'. Still, if you have granted correct Title or Positions, you will have in my eye slightly better standing on claiming of character that have official Position much lower than you - but only slightly.<br /> <br /> It's basically scenes like from <i>Harry Potter and Order of the Phoenix </i>- both Minister of Magic and Dumbledore have more or less the same Status 5 ( British Consilium ), only Minister have his official Title, so he makes legal procedures by his words. But Minister <i>still</i> is afraid of Dumbledore's speech, as he knows that what this wizard says has ENORMOUS impact on British mages on general, simple just him being <i>really liked</i> Principle of Hogwarts ( would be only Status 3 Title, but Dumbledore still would have like Status 5 on his sheet ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-30-2016, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T10:51:16-08:00","id":1024403,"title":"","content":"I would like to go a little further, to a general principle on the game stats.<br /> <br /> Merits aren't about describing your character. They are about the <i>advantages your character can reliably count on, from a mechanics stand point</i>. So it isn't what your character is or does by itself, but what it can do in the game, as a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:24:36-08:00","id":1024417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1024403#post1024403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to go a little further, to a general principle on the game stats.<br /> <br /> Merits aren't about describing your character. They are about the <i>advantages your character can reliably count on, from a mechanics stand point</i>. So it isn't what your character is or does by itself, but what it can do in the game, as a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an important point to keep in mind as well. To use another Social Merit as an example, a character doesn't have to have Anonymity to live off the grid. Anonymity just gives mechanical bonuses to a character who does live off the grid. A character doesn't have to have True Friend to have a deep, meaningful relationship with another character. True Friend just gives that relationship mechanical benefits. You don't have to have Resources 5 to be filthy stinking rich, Resources 5 just gives you a mechanical benefit for that money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:53:45-08:00","id":1024430,"title":"","content":"Bruce Wayne in the movie Batman Begins can be seen as an example of both 5dot 0dot paths. He has 5 dots in resources (spends money on expensive cars, buying restaurants on a whim &amp; dating supermodels) with 0 dots in status (the company CEO considers him an inconvenient waste at best). Drop his blatant spending to represent 0 dots in resources, but his 5 dots in status explains why Fox is willing to provide him with all of Batman's fancy equipment. Gaining material items through status just means that technically you will have to return it...eventually.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T05:36:34-08:00","id":1024725,"title":"","content":"CEO will get butlers and maids and super cars, but you won't be able to easily get that Resources 5 Obscure Occult thing without a roll.<br /> Trick is, your CEO Status probably will give you a bonus to the roll that will replace the &quot;instant resources spend no question asked&quot; ability of Resources. Your character is a super businessman with Status 5 and no resources, and needs lots of cash right now? Make a Persuasion roll to make a great business deal that will give you some cash, and if you fail, you can always ask for some interesting Condition to reflect using up your stuff.<br /> Its kind of like a Police Officer should probably get a gun as a part of their &quot;outfit&quot;, while a Journalist will not.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Basically, imagine that Status will give you a sphere of influence that allows to grab things that logically fall under it, while Resources is universal, no questions asked ability to procure things just based on their cost alone. Like, I'm not going to tax a character whose status is &quot;Famous independent journalist&quot; for expensive cameras, but she is not getting a gun out of it. She might, however, try to do a Streetwise roll with a Status bonus to represent &quot;yeah, I asked Bro-Gun to get me a gun, I did him a favor earlier by doing a nice article on his Bro-Music&quot; or something. Use it as an excuse to flesh out characters, not ban options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-31-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:23:26-08:00","id":1026017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1024403#post1024403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to go a little further, to a general principle on the game stats.<br /> <br /> Merits aren't about describing your character. They are about the <i>advantages your character can reliably count on, from a mechanics stand point</i>. So it isn't what your character is or does by itself, but what it can do in the game, as a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this true? It sounds like Merits are about describing your character:<br /> <br /> <i>Merits are important facets of your character that do not fall under other traits.</i> - p.26<br /> <br /> Wouldn't that suggest a character could, say, be an expert in Firearms but not have the dots to back it up? Be a genius at INT 1? Or to take it a step further, to be a Alder Vampire, but just not have BP, Disciplines, or Vitae? Unless you're suggesting that Merits are some special set of traits that don't have to match the character/follow the same rules as other traits (i.e. needing to exist).<br /> <br /> Which is... odd (to me), but okay. That idea raises a few questions, though.<br /> <br /> How, then, to address narrative discrepancy? Or what should the ST say to Player A with Resources 5 who is wondering why they have Resources 5 when Player B is wearing Dior and driving a McLaren on Resources 1?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong; I get what's being said. That a character could be good-looking or well-off, but just not get dice bonuses. It just seems like everyone would be good-looking, beach-bodied, rich, and well-connected. And if that's the case, doesn't it devalue those that have spent XP on those things? Narrative license is great, but doesn't that also drive players to just spending on powers and combat stats? If they can just narrate social qualities without spending?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:26:31-08:00","id":1026019,"title":"","content":"You totally can be a rich freelancer who uses Expression Rolls to generate Cash Equipment, without any kind of Resources Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:42:54-08:00","id":1026036,"title":"","content":"Sure, and the Availability and Procurement rider is a whole other can of worms. Letting one trait supersede another in every instance is just bad mechanics. <br /> <br /> You can just change the example if you like, to, say, Eidetic Memory, or Language, or Striking Looks, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:54:54-08:00","id":1026044,"title":"","content":"In 1E there was <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Merits,_Universal_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Luxury Merit</a> that let you live like a multimillionaire, without needing of stable Recourse to buy things. Seers of Throne were famous for using this on behalf of Exarchs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:28:40-08:00","id":1026070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026017#post1026017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this true? It sounds like Merits are about describing your character:<br /> <br /> <i>Merits are important facets of your character that do not fall under other traits.</i> - p.26</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, Merits can help describe your character, but they're not essential to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026017#post1026017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that suggest a character could, say, be an expert in Firearms but not have the dots to back it up? Be a genius at INT 1? Or to take it a step further, to be a Alder Vampire, but just not have BP, Disciplines, or Vitae?<br /> <br /> Unless you're suggesting that Merits are some special set of traits that don't have to match the character/follow the same rules as other traits (i.e. needing to exist).</div> </div> </div> </div>A character with no dots in Firearms won't be able to be an expert marksman because they'll be failing most of their Firearms rolls. Playing a genius character with Intelligence 1 would be difficult, since one of the traits that helps form your mental dice pools is low, but it could be made up for with more dots and Specialties in Mental Skills and maybe some relevant Merits. As for playing an elder vampire with only Blood Potency 1 and 3 dots of Disciplines, that's simple. You recently woke up from a long Torpor, which reduced your Blood Potency to 1, and the fog of ages has addled your memory, so while you may once have had more Disciplines, you've forgotten how to use them. I've had such characters in my games before, they can be quite fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026017#post1026017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is... odd (to me), but okay. That idea raises a few questions, though.<br /> <br /> How, then, to address narrative discrepancy? Or what should the ST say to Player A with Resources 5 who is wondering why they have Resources 5 when Player B is wearing Dior and driving a McLaren on Resources 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, player A can basically buy whatever he wants whenever he wants. Player B can only acquire equipment through other means, like leveraging Status or Allies. What kind of clothes he wears and what car he drives are basically just flavor text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026017#post1026017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get me wrong; I get what's being said. That a character could be good-looking or well-off, but just not get dice bonuses. It just seems like everyone would be good-looking, beach-bodied, rich, and well-connected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they That sounds like a horribly boring game. Don't your players what to try different sorts of characters?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026017#post1026017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if that's the case, doesn't it devalue those that have spent XP on those things? Narrative license is great, but doesn't that also drive players to just spending on powers and combat stats? If they can just narrate social qualities without spending?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't devalue that XP because it doesn't give you the benefits that the XP does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:48:24-08:00","id":1026088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026070#post1026070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they That sounds like a horribly boring game. Don't your players what to try different sorts of characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, a horror version of The OC or Jersey Shore sounds like fun to me. (being just a bit cheeky).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T14:10:00-08:00","id":1026157,"title":"","content":"On TV everyone has striking looks, drives a cool car or motorcycle and lives in a bungalow on the beach, not at the local YMCA. Seriously though if you can't see how a character can have zero dots in resources and still drive a supercar and live on the beach just watch Magnum P.I., that is exactly what he did.<br /> \u200bI'm willing to bet that it's the same at most tables, every girl has striking looks, every guy is built like Rambo and no one plays the guy who's pissing himself in the corner at the first sign of danger (or if they are it's because they actually like playing that kind of character). Explaining the discrepancies between narrative and mechanical is up to the ST and player, with those who really fail to do so doing so because they want to play at wish fulfilment.<br /> \u200bIt is also possible to use multiple merits to achieve the same ends, daddy's name can garner a lot of favors and a pretty girl never has to buy her own drinks, but those other merits should come with their own strings and limitations like daddy will always find out what you were up to and eventually the pretty girl is going to run into a guy who thinks he's entitled to more than just pleasant conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T15:37:29-08:00","id":1026187,"title":"","content":"A Merit states a fact about a character, and gives that fact concrete mechanical benefits. These two things are loosely coupled -- you can come up with situations where any given fact wouldn't have its corresponding benefits, and the benefits are often general enough that they can apply to various different facts.<br /> <br /> The Merit point economy isn't about restricting how many handsome billionaires there are in the world, it's about providing a manageable number of mechanical advantages for each player character. By default, I'd recommend that any Bruce Wayne or Christian Grey take Resources, but if a benefit isn't relevant to what a character gets up to in-game, then there's no reason for the player to pay points for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:48:35-08:00","id":1026261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026070#post1026070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for playing an elder vampire with only Blood Potency 1 and 3 dots of Disciplines, that's simple...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed the point. This isn't about reduced Potency, it's about the absolute non-existence of dots to correlate.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026070#post1026070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...basically just flavor text...</div> </div> </div> </div>That my 'elder vampire' would basically just be flavor text, when <i>mechanically </i>they were 100% pure mortal.<br /> <br /> Because if you're going to say one is 'okay' and one is not, then we really are talking about Merits being entirely different types of traits. Which is fine, if that's the system intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026070#post1026070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they That sounds like a horribly boring game. Don't your players what to try different sorts of characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had hundreds of players over the years, and I can factually, empirically state the <i>majority</i> of them prefer those qualities. If free, all the better.<br /> <br /> Honestly?<br /> <br /> This way sounds much, much <i>more boring</i>. If everyone can 'narrate' being whatever they want, then what's the point of spending XP or having any sort of goals that aren't powers/FX related? I can't imagine how a more permissive system would be less boring than a restrictive one, judged solely on the lowest common denominator -- which is going to be far and away higher on the permissive system.<br /> <br /> <b>But</b>!!!!<br /> <br /> If anyone remembers the old, old, old WW forums, I was a perennial bitchin'n'moanin' that there was no 'Word of God' to settle things like Steve Long did on the HERO forums. And now, RB has spoken, and given the 'Word of God' system intent.<br /> <br /> I'll need to truly ponder this!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T19:06:36-08:00","id":1026265,"title":"","content":"I don't think you know what &quot;empirically&quot; means. Because what you described is exactly the opposite of empirical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T19:34:45-08:00","id":1026273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026265#post1026265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you know what &quot;empirically&quot; means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd say the same about you, or that your reading comprehension skills could use some work. My statement refers to both <b>observation </b>and records (<b>evidence*</b>) of my players which can be filtered, sorted, and compared to generate statistics, including periods when 'simple cost' was used.<br /> <br /> To wit: that my statement referred to observation <i>rather than theory</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm <i>fairly</i> sure that's what 'empirical' means.<br /> <br /> <br /> * I've got several hundred character sheets and XP logs from several years of pbp. Sure, I suppose you could say they're unverifiable and that I've doctored or fabricated thousands of forum posts just to make random statements on <i>this </i>forum, but that seems like an awful lot of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","user":"grey_goose","date":". 01-03-2017, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:32:10-08:00","id":1026297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026017#post1026017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just seems like everyone would be good-looking, beach-bodied, rich, and well-connected. And if that's the case, doesn't it devalue those that have spent XP on those things? Narrative license is great, but doesn't that also drive players to just spending on powers and combat stats? If they can just narrate social qualities without spending?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want a system that would keep people from playing what they wanted to play.<br /> <br /> If people want to play good-looking, beach-bodied, rich, and well-connected people, why exactly does the system need to stop them? If you can't write a story around that, don't be the Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T22:54:57-08:00","id":1026345,"title":"","content":"<b>grey_goose</b>, <b>if ALL your players wants to play 'supermodels and hot millioners', why not simply give them 5 or 10 XP on start? </b>It would be more than enough to make any 'supermortal' character and will not take <i>anything</i> from the game as it is. CoD games are written to be realistic-ish on start, so if you do not like that, just move a starting point a level or two higher.<br /> <br /> Proper Batman is also no CoD starting character, not only because of his Resources/Status dilemma but from need of higher Skills, many Fighting Styles Merits and many more stats not in normal character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-04-2017, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:01:17-08:00","id":1026347,"title":"","content":"Existence of Striking Looks merit doesn't stop me from emulating effects of being pretty in other ways, which might include high traits (or normal traits balanced by lack of confidence, annoying personality and fashion choices that are aesthetics seppuku), dots in social skills, results of rolls to &quot;make myself pretty yo with that dicepool of daily self love&quot;, Conditions put into play by succeeding on a roll designed to give me &quot;LOOKING GOOD!&quot; Condition, or negotiating a Persistent Condition of &quot;Pretty Face, Pretty Troubles&quot; that balances some sort of benefits with Beat-worthy complications, which can include both things like unwanted interest of non-target sexuality or choking feeling that only thing I've got for myself are my looks and everything else about me is worthless, leading to some forced Willpower expenditures and penalties to some rolls.<br /> <br /> Just because there is Striking Looks merit, or Resources merit, doesn't mean you can't achieve a result of &quot;striking looking&quot; character by using many, many other tools given you by the system.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> For Expert Marksman, I would probably go for a character that has some kind of Status related to their Expert Marksmanship (I assume you are talking about a sport person, not a sniper or something) and use the bonus from it to enhance non combat uses of guns, in order to highlight the fact that shooting stuff in controlled and friendly environment might work totally differently for my character than desperately trying to put down that GrimEater.<br /> <br /> You can also go for generally low Firearms but high dots in Marksmanship Style.<br /> <br /> Or you could just play a character who is Expert Marksman but got low chances to succeed on rolls, and have fun explaining why they fail using something different than &quot;incompetent&quot; each time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-04-2017, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:24:59-08:00","id":1026353,"title":"","content":"This game, like maybe every game outside of Traveler, was designed to create starting characters who are fresh out of childhood with very limited experience and development. If your player really wants to write up a specific character that requires more merits or specific skills, and if everyone else at the table agrees, then I would recommend the two of you sit down and design their character first then figure out the points required second.<br /> \u200bPersonally, unless the characters are supposed to be untried teens, I like to give my players bonus points to start with the caveat that they can only be spent on none splat related skills and merits. I also ask that they provide a story (narrative) reason why their character would have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T00:04:35-08:00","id":1026372,"title":"","content":"What? Starting characters aren't really fresh out of childhood. Remember that 2 dots in a skill is now &quot;professional&quot; level. Starting characters get TONS of training under their belt from skills alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:34:22-08:00","id":1026567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026345#post1026345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>grey_goose</b>, if ALL your players wants to play 'supermodels and hot millioners', why not simply give them 5 or 10 XP on start?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they get more than that to start. 30XP to start and the average player picks up around 7XP per calendar month.<br /> <br /> <i>My objection isn't about keeping people from playing what they want to play</i>. At all.<br /> <br /> It's about keeping things fair and maintaining a semblance of a baseline. With lots of players doing 'soft', or social, <b>PvP</b>, jockeying for status or building alliances is as much about perception as it is about reality. If all the Carthians are driving Koenigseggs on Resources 0, then the perception of the Invictus amassing wealth is devalued. <br /> <br /> Which I think is the disconnect. I'm not involved in single troupe games which are primarily PvE. I've got multiple coteries/cabals/motleys in detentes that are pushing each other up/tearing each other down. I'm not trying to be obtuse and hold my players down, I'm trying to sort out &quot;Rules of Engagement&quot; for them clawing each others eyes out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's why I'm probably more concerned with the relationships between traits/costs/in-game impact.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:45:57-08:00","id":1026727,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3557\" data-vbnamecard=\"3557\">grey_goose</a>, I think I'm starting to see what's your concern. And since no one achieved to deliver the point, I'll try it at another light.<br /> <br /> The key to it seems to be your last statement: &quot;the relationships between traits/costs/in-game impact&quot;.<br /> <br /> What we are trying to explain is precisely that: Merits aren't about describing the character. They tie at some level to the character, but the way of this tie is up to the people playing.<br /> <br /> Instead, they are about <u><b>the relationship between traits/costs/in-game impact</b></u>.<br /> <br /> Character A can be described as filthy rich, but without a single dot in Resources in the sheet. Character B can be described as living in the streets, homeless, but be assigned Resources 4 in the sheet. Certainly, the relation between sheet and actual character have to be described, no one argues that and you see our efforts to do so in the examples. Character A can be described as somehow having no saves at all, the money being destined in such a way as for the character to effectively bring nothing to the table, while Character B can be described as able to do its trade in such a manner that the money just flows whenever needed, the kind of person who don't need to be rich to get things when needed.<br /> <br /> All said and done, that is, once given the description, things work like this: Character A can be shown as owning prettier things and eating at fancy restaurants, <i>as long as it isn't really relevant for the chronicle</i>. If at any point it becomes relevant, ST and player have to find any reasonable explanation for the character to not have such benefits, anymore. Or to keep them through means that should be available to every other character (maybe everyone gets a roll to find a way to attend the fancy dinner, and the character need an equivalent roll to convince the accountant at this time that the money is for a good enough cause). Character B won't have pretty things most of the time, but certainly can get them if really needed. At the core, a character gets as benefit in the game what is somehow paid for.<br /> <br /> So, the core principle is exactly the relation you worry about. A merit isn't a description of the character, but of what the character can get of the game. The description that is relevant isn't of the character itself, but of the relation between character and mechanical benefit, and it is let loose, yes. Tying it strongly to a fixed description is both restrictive and ineffective, since both context and player ability can change drastically what a given description entails in the game. A loose description focused on actual mechanics gives you a clear goal for the benefits of the trait while let ST and players manage with more freedom the descriptive details as needed to achieve said goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:48:51-08:00","id":1026733,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you do have to adopt different strategies if you have more than one core cast.<br /> <br /> The core rules are written with the assumption of between two and six players (including the ST), with a single core cast that both works together and conflicts with each other, and that develops interpersonal relationships that can help, hinder, or flavor their external goals at different times. They're also written with the assumption that players are collaborative out of character, such that if my character and Eddy's are both trying to become Sheriff, neither of us is going to be angry at the other in real life if we lose. The player/GM responsibilities sections in the core book intros are very much written with this in mind.<br /> <br /> Costing and limitations are aimed at providing an optimal number of benefits and/or options for core gameplay, and keeping those even between characters, primarily in terms of spotlight opportunities. Obviously, they also take into account assumptions of overall capability -- an average Chronicles of Darkness character wins some and loses some. Whether they win or lose more is a chronicle-level style choice, but they always move forward and experience positive and negative consequences from their experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 01-04-2017, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:20:08-08:00","id":1026771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026733#post1026733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you do have to adopt different strategies if you have more than one core cast.<br /> <br /> The core rules are written with the assumption of between two and six players (including the ST), with a single core cast that both works together and conflicts with each other, and that develops interpersonal relationships that can help, hinder, or flavor their external goals at different times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. <i>Interesting</i>. I guess I carried that fact that 1E/MET rules were identical except for dice/resolution forward without realizing TT was really drilling down into the actual table top as a logical unit.<br /> <br /> Thanks for enlightening me!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T18:23:01-08:00","id":1026796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026771#post1026771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. <i>Interesting</i>. I guess I carried that fact that 1E/MET rules were identical except for dice/resolution forward without realizing TT was really drilling down into the actual table top as a logical unit.<br /> <br /> Thanks for enlightening me!</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were doing MET 2e, I would take a pretty different approach from what I've done with tabletop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T18:27:19-08:00","id":1026798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026796#post1026796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were doing MET 2e, I would take a pretty different approach from what I've done with tabletop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Words cannot describe how much I would love such a product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:38:10-08:00","id":1027694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026567#post1026567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's about keeping things fair and maintaining a semblance of a baseline. With lots of players doing 'soft', or social, <b>PvP</b>, jockeying for status or building alliances is as much about perception as it is about reality. If all the Carthians are driving Koenigseggs on Resources 0, then the perception of the Invictus amassing wealth is devalued.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the big reason I have wealth go hand-in-hand with Resources. The Merit is a lot sexier for players when you get to tie flavor as well as mechanics to it. There are probably entire sessions that go by when the Resources 5 PC isn't dropping around Resources 5 levels of cash, but being able to describe one's means of transport as a private helicopter ride still gives a cool return for the Merit.<br /> <br /> I've also found that players who describe themselves as being rich or attended by legions of followers will also want to use them in helpful ways that don't necessarily call for dice rolls/bonuses or other clear mechanics. It's more fun to see players using Merits in helpful/story-driving ways to think up convoluted reasons for why their described background elements have to remain window dressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T04:14:22-08:00","id":1029546,"title":"","content":"Sorry for not participating lately in the thread I created, been on holidays. Thank you to you all for your answers and the discussions, they have helped me a lot! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026727#post1026727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key to it seems to be your last statement: &quot;the relationships between traits/costs/in-game impact&quot;.<br /> <br /> A merit isn't a description of the character, but of what the character can get of the game. The description that is relevant isn't of the character itself, but of the relation between character and mechanical benefit, and it is let loose, yes. Tying it strongly to a fixed description is both restrictive and ineffective, since both context and player ability can change drastically what a given description entails in the game. A loose description focused on actual mechanics gives you a clear goal for the benefits of the trait while let ST and players manage with more freedom the descriptive details as needed to achieve said goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This thing is what really has been hard on me. I mean, I amb an old school RPG player and I am used to pay (in game terms) and keep track of money, for example, the famous gold coins of D&amp;D, or credits in Star Wars.<br /> <br /> With the Resources Merit, what it came to my mind was &quot;ah, I can aquire an item or service of value X each session, and an item/service of value X-2 always&quot;, and I though about it as if it where money, then I though money = social class. And I think is a mistake that most CoD players have done, do, and will do due to how the merit is described in the books.<br /> <br /> Seeing it as &quot;what can you aquire mechanically when the item/service IS RELEVANT to the story&quot; change things a lot. And if we say that it has not to be acquired exactly with money, better. A person of resources is not allways a rich one, no? That low class man has resources 4 because he knows people, have friends with better luck than him (not represented by allies because Allies give another type of mechanical benefit), and when he needs to go to an expensive concert where something important is going to happen, he has a friend that can provide him with the tickets.<br /> <br /> So, all depends on how you describe it.<br /> <br /> And I think the same is valid for Safe House and other merits. You can have a neat survelliance equipment in your mansion, but when is really put at test it fails in a misserable manner when IS RELEVANT to the story due to that Safe House 0.<br /> <br /> This gives more open dessign possibilities for characters. Resources 0 doen't mean you live on the getto. I have players of Mage 2nd that recently yelled to have to spend merit points on resources, they were seeing their characters living under a bridge with resources 0 (old school gamers, too).<br /> <br /> I only have one petition and is that, if possible, in next books, make this clarification of the merits (and print it in bold style), that they are mechanical benefits when the situation is relevant. That resources doesn't mean money, but the ability to aquire things/services when needed, that status is not position but influence, and that all are only mechanicall benefits, not narrative limitations, and only when is relevant to the story, not to the metagame/background of the characters. You can play a Bruce Wayne but you have to go nuts the same way as young and poor Peter Parker when you want to aquire something of resources 3 when your resources are at 1. You can be a respected teacher at the university and gained a Nobel, but when you need something, for you is not easier than for any other teacher to get help and resources from the highers when is relevant for the story (Staus 0 == Influence 0).<br /> <br /> Thank to you all!! Really! ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 01-10-2017, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T05:13:47-08:00","id":1030009,"title":"","content":"There is my 5 cents! I have thoughts but i dont wont start another topic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thing is what really has been hard on me. I mean, I amb an old school RPG player and I am used to pay (in game terms) and keep track of money, for example, the famous gold coins of D&amp;D, or credits in Star Wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have same exact problem.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;ah, I can aquire an item or service of value X each session, and an item/service of value X-2 always&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As homebrew i give to my players with resources merit buy points (1 per <i>story </i>for 1 dot 2 - 2 dots, 4 - 3 dot, 7 - 4 dot, 12 - 5 dot). And they can be spend it to buy things on their price (Availability) as described in book. This represent the amount of cash available to them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;what can you aquire mechanically when the item/service IS RELEVANT to the story&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I alow such use of Resources Merit only on thing which can be purchased (available on market) - you can't buy voodoo doll, you can only craft it or get it from some one particular (for the mutual service, if necessary).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resources 0 doen't mean you live on the getto</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no people with steady income and without ability pour money on problem. If person have money for day to day live then he have money to spend. As <i>Morton's Fork </i>there you can always draw money but at what cost?<br /> if PC does not have Resources Merit i grant it to him with one of two conditions: Dept or Loan (persistent). Debt for one dot of merit and Loan for 2 or 3 dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Debt.</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">it is good if you you have a debt to the relatives. It does not add to the popularity, but you have a chance to remain relatively intact. But what if any relatives live in another town, city or even another state? To whom can you turn to? It's good if you have a friend or two. But what if you does not? Gloomy dude is not exactly the best choice.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: decide not to give money back or not being able to give It back or repay debt not with money.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: make withdrew debt by all means.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Loan</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Such amount of money you cant just simply gather from your relatives. This amount of money can be obtained only from the one who has them. And that amount of money is not accepted to forgive. It's bad for business. Even if the money were taken in the bank, in the best case the bank can sue you in case of refusal to give it. In the best case.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> pay interest or expire payment.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> pay the debt off... or in one of not so bright days wake up in an ice bath without one kidney.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And for meaning of paying interest there <b>Cash </b>tilt. It's grand one use of one-dot version of Resources Merit. Possible Sources: theft, looting, honest work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T10:47:07-08:00","id":1030128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030009#post1030009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no people with steady income and without ability pour money on problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incredibly untrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:12:16-08:00","id":1030169,"title":"","content":"Why so? For me it's question of resolve. If you have rights of possession on something you can abandon this for the money (Sanctity of Merits rule). If you say about Bruce Wayne example look for it as how little self-restraint. &quot;Oh, boy! I need that auctioning enchanted claymore. Unfortunately for its i will have to refuse to buy another Ferrari&quot; If you can afford some lifestyle then you can bye what you can afford in time of need.<br /> It's the question of sacrificing something for attain something else. Can you dare at that?<br /> Lets try this: you always can use Sanctity of Merits rule for transferring dots of social network merits (as Allies or Status) in Resource but never vice versa.<br /> <br /> And it's not as if I did not agree with the written by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026727#post1026727\"><b>monteparnas</b></a><b>: </b>i myself have PC who have income not from Resource Merit but by Status Merit (state employee) for his lifestyle. If he begins to blatantly take bribes, then it certainly will increase his income ... With the chances of certain consequences. I say you always can reallocate your income.<br /> And you can always get into debt.<br /> <br /> How to say so? Not that I was sorry to give character his income. Just a character with no dots in Resources asking for trouble related to his income.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-11-2017, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:38:33-08:00","id":1030189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030169#post1030169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you always can use Sanctity of Merits rule for transferring dots of social network merits (as Allies or Status) in Resource but never vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source? Or is this your house rule to make the rules align better with your worldview/gameplay style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:46:36-08:00","id":1030193,"title":"","content":"fresh homebrew rule for sake of making point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:51:18-08:00","id":1030262,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12029\" data-vbnamecard=\"12029\">OsuNeko</a>, I had some trouble with your first post here, but the second clarified things enough for me.<br /> <br /> I do agree with most of what you said. At most, I wouldn't say that you can't use Sanctity of Merits to exchange Resources for Social Merits. I would only ask for a good explanation for any exchange of Merits, and a good reason to let it be. Probably I would limit it to downtime between stories.<br /> <br /> And I really liked the two sample Conditions! I would probably make the Beat a little more streamlined, but not only I liked, I'm going to test it on my next game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:54:31-08:00","id":1030448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say that you can't use Sanctity of Merits to exchange Resources for Social Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making friends is harder then making money. Friends can be friend only once, after that they can accept you but never trust you again.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would probably make the Beat a little more streamlined</div> </div> </div> </div>In Debt Condition, IMHO, beat only can obtained if don't returning money - experience has shown that is too simple just returning money. For Loan Condition you need to pay every chapter or story (depending on to whom character is obliged) - it's making it harder to pay off (and hove mach should be payed depending on ST).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-12-2017, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T04:03:52-08:00","id":1030514,"title":"","content":"Notying says you need to get friendly with the same friends. Most social Merits doesn't deal with friends anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T04:37:02-08:00","id":1030519,"title":"","content":"imagine how NPCs will feel when their dots will be moved to the Resources? It is for the players it's just Sanctity of Merit. But for NPCs that is something barely acceptable: you not just downgrade your merit, you make them do something that makes them turn away from you. Money does not remember evil, but people do. Here you need to understand that you do not simply transfer your wealth from one bed to another, but the fact that it causes social consequences. If you you were just hired employees that you paid a salary, and then decided to dismiss some of them then hire new ones - no problem (Staff to Resources and Resources to Staff). But what if your informant was forced to move out without your support? Suddenly, your friends from the gang that robbed a jewelry at your request, were hunted down and arrested. They do not hold a grudge against you, but you have to wait before they will be released.<br /> The point there is that social networks can not be simply bought (where should 'simply' stand in this sentence?). You have to build bridges: to find out to whom the request with which you can contact, who like whats, but not just come up and say &quot;hey, dude, there's your cash, and now you're working for me&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T04:47:59-08:00","id":1030521,"title":"","content":"Sanctity of Merits doesn't necessarily mean that you have to exchange one Merit for another in the game. You've lost your Resources for whatever reason. You can get Contacts from a group completely unrelated to what happened to your Resources, just like you've payed XP for it, but since you have a few freed up Merit dots you could use them instead of XP that you could put on stuff that isn't Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T05:13:29-08:00","id":1030523,"title":"","content":"Well it's depend of storytelling manner: you may approve only thing which has been acquired through game. Or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T06:38:59-08:00","id":1030548,"title":"","content":"So you created a new house rule to make a point about your argument? At that point my mind exploded. And yes, there's people with a steady income, who can't pour money into a problem. Almost anyone with a bank loan big enough, that majority of their income goes to repaying that is in such a case. They can't just say &quot;i'm not gonna pay the bank.&quot; effectively, they're resources 0., even tho, they could have a huge house and a ferrari. <br /> <br /> Them deciding to sell those objects for some cash is not something Resources merit is supposed to cover. The merit itself says that it's supposed to cover DISPOSABLE cash, and your bank loans are not disposable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T07:28:53-08:00","id":1030571,"title":"","content":"Everyone can &quot;choose&quot; to not pay for a lot of stuff, but a lot of people (absolutely no everyone, but far from nobody) can only do so at the risk of losing their home, their job, having to starve for the rest of the month or putting themselves into the kind of debt that has a huge risk of leading to greater poverty. It's not really a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T09:03:14-08:00","id":1030610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's choice in the world where you literally can become someones pray.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They can't just say &quot;i'm not gonna pay the bank.&quot; effectively, they're resources 0., even tho, they could have a huge house and a ferrari.<br /> <br /> Them deciding to sell those objects for some cash is not something Resources merit is supposed to cover. The merit itself says that it's supposed to cover DISPOSABLE cash, and your bank loans are not disposable.</div> </div> </div> </div>For that there is two homerule (which i already use) condition for loans. You acquire DISPOSABLE cash but with chances to lose ALL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T09:03:20-08:00","id":1030611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030548#post1030548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Them deciding to sell those objects for some cash is not something Resources merit is supposed to cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. We're having a conversation about Resources, which is explicitly <i>extra</i> disposable <i>income</i>, not 'having money'.<br /> Instead of making bizarre houserules, use Cash Equipment (aka 'having money') for what it was made for, and Resources for what it was made for, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T09:17:41-08:00","id":1030614,"title":"","content":"I forgot all about them. I feel like an idiot. But it's said &quot;For more complex uses, consider it a single month\u2019s allotment of the same Resources&quot;.<br /> As such, it does not change my position. We do not change Merit on equipment. We change Merit on Merit. After acquiring of some cash you can deposit it or play on Forex (if some skill presented).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:38:19-08:00","id":1030659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030614#post1030614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot all about them. I feel like an idiot. But it's said &quot;For more complex uses, consider it a single month\u2019s allotment of the same Resources&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means it's 'spent' (mechanically) in the same way the merit is, not that it fills the same narrative role. Resources remain disposable income. Cash is cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T09:19:59-08:00","id":1031618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030548#post1030548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you created a new house rule to make a point about your argument? At that point my mind exploded. And yes, there's people with a steady income, who can't pour money into a problem. Almost anyone with a bank loan big enough, that majority of their income goes to repaying that is in such a case. They can't just say &quot;i'm not gonna pay the bank.&quot; effectively, they're resources 0., even tho, they could have a huge house and a ferrari.<br /> <br /> Them deciding to sell those objects for some cash is not something Resources merit is supposed to cover. The merit itself says that it's supposed to cover DISPOSABLE cash, and your bank loans are not disposable.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I could understand, OsuNeko's point wasn't that the character needs Resources to have stuff, but that having stuff is a descriptive way to justify acquiring Conditions or using Sanctity of Merits to obtain stuff. That is, again, as I understood it, the point in saying that the person can find a way to access the money.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12029\" data-vbnamecard=\"12029\">OsuNeko</a>, social Merits aren't so straightforward, either. Nor is Sanctity of Merits.<br /> <br /> First, imagine this: a character can decide to spend a lot of money going to clubs, bribing club guards, and stuff, just to get used to the club scene and be known enough in the scene. The character effectively changes a dot on Resources for Barfly. The character can donate money in a regular basis to an organization, or otherwise use the money to financially back-up them, effectively changing Resources for Allies. Or put a lot of money into the right hands for information and change Resources for Contacts, or even bribe the way through the meandres of the organization to change Resources for Status.<br /> <br /> But Sanctity of Merits isn't about this, either way. Changing Merits around is an option that the ST can and should grant only with certain care. Preferably between stories, not just between chapters. Maybe not at all, because this isn't the core of Sanctity of Merits. The core of Sanctity of Merits is that &quot;nothing that happens in the story should reduce the ratings on Merits of the character sheet&quot;. It isn't about versatility, but about protection. The player is guaranteed to keep all the points spent. So, if something in story happens to somehow destroy something from the character sheet, the player have the right to be refund on every XP point that Merit was worth to spend anew. The most common thing in the sheet to be destroyed are Merits, and the simplest thing to repurpose the XP are also Merits, and overall is recommended that the ST gives preference for the points being repurposed in the same category. Hence the name Sanctity of Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:14:33-08:00","id":1031645,"title":"","content":"I think I've completely lost track of the discussion here. What are we talking about? Cause it looks like there are two or three completely separate things being discussed at once here and it's causing a lot of confusion.<br /> <br /> Re: having consistent income and not having disposable income. Yes, this is entirely possible and quite common in real life. There are plenty of people with jobs that provide them enough money to pay their bills and feed themselves and/or their dependents, but little to none left over after that to spend on things they want for themselves. In game terms, this is what having a consistent source of income and no dots in Resources looks like. Remember, Resources doesn't represent any and all money, it specifically represents <i>disposable income</i>. Money you are receiving on a regular basis, in excess of what it costs to keep your basic needs met. Money that you can freely spend on shot guns, rock salt, antique ritual knives, and all the other weird shit characters in Chronicles of Darkness end up needing.<br /> <br /> Re: Resources vs. Cash. Resources, as mentioned above, represents money you can regularly spend every month on things beyond keeping up with your recurring expenses. Mechanically, this is represented by an ability to acquire a specific Availability worth of equipment and services each month (or each chapter). Cash represents money you have that is not part of your regular income, and can be spent once to acquire a specific Availability worth of equipment and services.<br /> <br /> Re: Sanctity of Merits. This is specifically something that exists to protect players' experience investments. If you spent 5 Experiences (in other words, roughly 6 game sessions worth of character advancement) to get Resources 5, representing your character's job at a fancy law firm, and then the law firm gets blown up as part of the plot and your character loses their job, you as a player don't lose that 6 weeks worth of experiences. You no longer have those Resources dots, because it doesn't make sense in the narrative to have disppsable income from a job that no longer exists, but you get those 5 Experiences back and can spend them on other Merits. It does not allow players to exchange one Merit for another on a whim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:58:09-08:00","id":1031682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is entirely possible and quite common in real life</div> </div> </div> </div>It's dire situation. Shit happens. Less or more but happens. And maybe <i>Darkness</i> throw a glimpse when it happens. My point here.<br /> When you have zero balance on end of month you are less likely <i>to </i><i>buy</i> a solution. You should sacrifice something to maintain balance. And how big Status Merit of the character, so deep his problem.<br /> And if [my] players do not wont problems from this side they should take Resource Merit [so as not to tempt me].<br /> Well, this is not true for the homeless. But imagine Bruce Wayne, who has his Batcave repledge thrice. Or mediocre clerk, who was going to divorce. Or a drug dealer who carries cash [after deal] [and much more than he would leave for himself].<br /> Shit happens. Often.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sanctity of Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seek here another way to use this rule: willingly (as far as it is acceptable) transfer social (and other what can be lost) merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-14-2017, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:05:15-08:00","id":1031688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031682#post1031682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's dire situation. Shit happens. Less or more but happens. And maybe <i>Darkness</i> throw a glimpse when it happens. My point there.<br /> When you have zero balance on end of month you are less likely <i>to </i><i>buy</i> a solution. You should sacrifice something to maintain balance. And how big Status Merit of the character, so deep his problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you are saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031682#post1031682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if [my] players do not wont problems from this side they should take Resource Merit [so as not to tempt me].</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be yet more evidence of your group having a contentious &quot;player vs. GM&quot; dynamic. No offense, but I would not want to play in a game run by you if the players and the GM are working against each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031682#post1031682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is not true for the homeless. But imagine Bruce Wayne, who has his Batcave repledge thrice. Or mediocre clerk, whom was going to divorce. Or a drug dealer who carries cash [after deal].</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine what about them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031682#post1031682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shit happens. Often.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but I'm not understanding what it has to do with the topic we are discussing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031682#post1031682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seek here another way to use this rule: willingly (as far as it is acceptable) transfer social (and other what can be lost) merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to use it that way, go ahead. That's not what it's meant for though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:20:26-08:00","id":1031700,"title":"","content":"They are talking about 'selling off' social merits to get the Resources merit to represent getting money in the story. Probably comes from a system where die-hard tracking of every gold piece matters.<br /> <br /> This is why I mentioned just using Cash equipment for selling stuff off, or getting money some other way. They want to use merits and houserule everything to D&amp;D and back instead of engaging with the system as written.<br /> <br /> I don't think there can be much further productive discussion at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:59:25-08:00","id":1031720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what you are saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Steady&quot; income only sounds as it. In practice there fluctuation you can observe: inflation (somewhere in the world it is more than 2%), emergencies (remember the tsunami in Malaysia, when the Samsungs plant was destroyed? HHD price has risen twice), mortgage/oil bubbles. Some Global Shit. Well, when you live on the <i>mainland</i>, neither financial nor water tsunami does not gets personally you. However, they are much spoil steadiness of income.<br /> And when Global Shit synchronized with personal shit (wrecked leg without health insurance, or court expenses, or lover of your lover has learned that she has a lover) then problem may appear. And what will you do when your &quot;steady&quot; income falls due to global shit while you lay down in hospital chamber?<br /> Or another situation in which you SUDDENLY no longer have enough money for your lifestyle.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to be yet more evidence of your group having a contentious &quot;player vs. GM&quot; dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>They ask for this. Literally. Not as trolls but as decent players. They ask for some <i>interlude</i> (one-chapter story) between <i>stories</i>. Inventing their problems - one of the ways to fill them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offense, but I would not want to play in a game run by you if the players and the GM are working against each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are still not familiar with Tyoma. You ever played Dark Soul? maybe it's his influence.<br /> But personally, I prefer this style, where players do not fall into the situation but enter them themselves.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine what about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>What should be done with the mortgaged property, in case of non-payment of debt. Or when your wife's lawyer knows divorce inside out. Or how to punish the guilty (after losing all revenue) in the criminal group.<br /> All these sudden situations can<i> be purchased</i>. Except last... But if he has enough time then drug dealer can present his money instead lost ones.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true, but I'm not understanding what it has to do with the topic we are discussing.</div> </div> </div> </div>For People with high status problems are less common, but when they occur they far exceed those that occur for ordinary people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-14-2017, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T12:37:52-08:00","id":1031735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031720#post1031720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Steady&amp;quot; income only sounds as it. In practice there fluctuation you can observe: inflation (somewhere in the world it is more than 2%), emergencies (remember the tsunami in Malaysia, when the Samsungs plant was destroyed? HHD price has risen twice), mortgage/oil bubbles. Some Global Shit. Well, when you live on the <i>mainland</i>, neither financial nor water tsunami does not gets personally you. However, they are much spoil steadiness of income.<br /> And when Global Shit synchronized with personal shit (wrecked leg without health insurance, or court expenses, or lover of your lover has learned that she has a lover) then problem may appear. And what will you do when your &amp;quot;steady&amp;quot; income falls due to global shit while you lay down in hospital chamber?<br /> Or another situation in which you SUDDENLY no longer have enough money for your lifestyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're a character in a Chronicles of Darkness game? You lose those Resources dots and have the experiences refunded via Sanctity of Merits. If your income isn't steady or isn't disposable, then it isn't represented by the Resources Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031720#post1031720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They ask for this. Literally. Not as trolls but as decent players. They ask for some <i>interlude</i> (one-chapter story) between <i>stories</i>. Inventing their problems - one of the ways to fill them.<br /> <br /> You are still not familiar with Tyoma. You ever played Dark Soul? maybe it's his influence.<br /> But personally, I prefer this style, where players do not fall into the situation but enter them themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gather that you like it. I'm just saying, seems like an unpleasant experience to me, personally. I love Dark Souls, and I enjoy challenge in an RPG, but in an RPG I want to be working together with the GM to insure a fun and challenging experience, not competing to thwart each others' plans. But whatever, if you and your players like it, have fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031720#post1031720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What should be done with the mortgaged property, in case of non-payment of debt. Or when your wife's lawyer knows divorce inside out. Or how to punish the guilty (after losing all revenue) in the criminal group.</div> </div> </div> </div>You lose the house, lose a lot in the divorce, or the criminal gets put in jail. Again, what does this have to do with the topic we are discussing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031720#post1031720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All these sudden situations can<i> be purchased</i>. Except last... But if he has enough time then drug dealer can present his money instead lost ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;These situations can be purchased&quot; doesn't make sense to me. Could you try rephrasing this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031720#post1031720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For People with high status problems are less common, but when they occur they far exceed those that occur for ordinary people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is true, but what does it have to do with the Resources Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T12:49:50-08:00","id":1031743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031735#post1031735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your income isn't steady or isn't disposable, then it isn't represented by the Resources Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the part I feel is getting lost in translation somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T12:57:09-08:00","id":1031747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;These situations can be purchased&quot; doesn't make sense to me. Could you try rephrasing this?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have some saving or your income exceed expenses you can withdrew loan, have share after divorce enough big for you, or bribe off from jail.<br /> But you can do all of this only if you have disposable resources (ie Resources Merit). Pour money on problem.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">isn't steady or isn't disposable</div> </div> </div> </div>This &quot;or&quot; - a logical addition or logical multiplication?<br /> Ie if it's only a steady income, the character must have this Merritt? Or it is mandatory should be stable AND disposable income?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-14-2017, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:10:29-08:00","id":1031761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031747#post1031747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have some saving or your income exceed expenses you can withdrew loan, have share after divorce enough big for you, or bribe off from jail.<br /> But you can do all of this only if you have disposable resources (ie Resources Merit).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Resources Merit isn't just any disposable money. It has to be <i>both</i> disposable <i>and</i> consistent. If you lose your source of income, you lose the Merit, because the source of income is no longer consistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031747#post1031747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This &amp;quot;or&amp;quot; - a logical addition or logical subtraction?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a source of income is not both disposable and consistent, then it shouldn't be represented by the Resources Merit. Therefore, if it is disposable but not consistent, or if it is consistent but not disposable, then it shouldn't be represented by the Resources Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:18:23-08:00","id":1031765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Resources Merit isn't just any disposable money. It has to be <i>both</i> disposable <i>and</i> consistent. If you lose your source of income, you lose the Merit, because the source of income is no longer consistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what if character does not have this Merit but only his Status dots? or you wont to say that character with Status Merit have authority to pressure?<br /> <br /> Damn. I was again led off the way. I think I begin to argue again for the sake of dispute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-14-2017, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:28:28-08:00","id":1031772,"title":"","content":"Put it this way, you have a job that gives you money in excess of what you need to live at your current pace. That's Resources. You have a wad of a few hundred dollars that you stole from a bank in your pocket. That's the Cash equipment. You have a nice car collection. That's it's own Equipment. You have a respected position in a company that allows you to call favours and influence policy. That's Status. You take a pay cut, you lose Resources. You get XP, you decide you want to use that XP to learn Firearms skill. You don't have a gun, but you also don't have the Resources anymore to buy it, so you give up your Cash for it. You still have your Status though, so you can make sure that Jeffreys the Janitor looks the other way when he finds you mishandling documents in another department, because you're a respected higher up and can get him fired. These are all separate ideas. <br /> <br /> So you have the disposable wealth that you get in a constant basis, that's Resources. You have disposable wealth you got from a one time deal, that's Cash. You have non-disposable wealth that's it's own Equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:44:21-08:00","id":1031786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031765#post1031765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what if character does not have this Merit but only his Status dots? or you wont to say that character with Status Merit have authority to pressure?</div> </div> </div> </div>A character with high Status in an organization that would pay well, but no dots in Resources would have an income that is consistent, but not disposable. They make lots of money, but it all goes to paying for expenses. If economic pressure causes them to lose that job, they might lose the Status dots representing it (which would be refunded with Sanctity of Merits). They would also lose their source of income, and potentially anything they owned that relied on that income. For example, if they lost their house, they would lose their Housing Equipment and potentially any Safe Place dots invested in securing it (the latter being refunded with Sanctity of Merits). If they lost their car, they would lose the Vehicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T01:24:05-08:00","id":1032041,"title":"","content":"Ok, some sleep should help.<br /> I try to say, what would character (with Status Merit not with Resource Merit) should do when shit hit the fan? He does not have his disposable money or another form of wealth (he does not have Resource merit) - he only have what he can afford by his Status. He will try automatically press by his authority? In common pace in dire situation most people try to buy off from this, because other methods much harder.<br /> <br /> This topic popup with question: should character backup his status with money (and vise versa)? Most answers sound as &quot;No, he does not&quot; with foundation for this describer as &quot;he has zero balance on end of month&quot; or &quot;he does not have disposable resources&quot; which looks synonymous. Such answer implies that character have some income which steadiness not insured (who is it guaranteed?). And what will character do, if he loose his income (when he does not have Resource merit at all)?<br /> If he is a &quot;good&quot; ST he does not use such cheap tricks. If he is &quot;evil&quot; ST then he not just use such stunt but worsens situation by all means combining all similar factors (when presence of privilege is not guaranteed). But &quot;realistic&quot; ST not simple use but permits...<br /> Damn. Sleep helped. Writing has helped realize that it is self-evident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-15-2017, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T01:53:57-08:00","id":1032044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032041#post1032041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, some sleep should help.<br /> I try to say, what would character (with Status Merit not with Resource Merit) should do when shit hit the fan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sell off the equipment he can (vehicles, houses, whatever) in exchange for the Cash equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T04:14:12-08:00","id":1032076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032041#post1032041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This topic popup with question: should character backup his status with money (and vise versa)? Most answers sound as &quot;No, he does not&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, nobody I can see is saying this. The answer to, &quot;should a character backup his Status with Resources, or Resources with Status?&quot; is, &quot;whatever makes sense for the character keeping in mind that 'no' is a viable option in the system.&quot; followed by explanations of why &quot;no&quot; works in the system even when it seems like it might not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T05:50:23-08:00","id":1032100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1031786#post1031786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character with high Status in an organization that would pay well, but no dots in Resources would have an income that is consistent, but not disposable. They make lots of money, but it all goes to paying for expenses. If economic pressure causes them to lose that job, they might lose the Status dots representing it (which would be refunded with Sanctity of Merits). They would also lose their source of income, and potentially anything they owned that relied on that income. For example, if they lost their house, they would lose their Housing Equipment and potentially any Safe Place dots invested in securing it (the latter being refunded with Sanctity of Merits). If they lost their car, they would lose the Vehicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, any time they want to use money from that job, they need to make a roll in order to procure equipment: Cash. Which of course can fail.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And before someone says that &quot;procuring equipment &quot;Cash&quot; destroys niche of Resources!&quot; : Resources are very, VERY good at this thing. Infinitely better than anything roll based. It's niche isn't &quot;ability to generate money&quot;, it's niche is &quot;ability to 100% sure generate infinite amounts of Resources-X money and less infinite but still 100% guaranteed amount of money=Resources&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-15-2017, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:07:05-08:00","id":1032362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032076#post1032076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, nobody I can see is saying this. The answer to, &quot;should a character backup his Status with Resources, or Resources with Status?&quot; is, &quot;whatever makes sense for the character keeping in mind that 'no' is a viable option in the system.&quot; followed by explanations of why &quot;no&quot; works in the system even when it seems like it might not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he just wanted to use &quot;must&quot; instead of &quot;should&quot;. &quot;May&quot;, &quot;Can&quot;, &quot;Should&quot; and &quot;Must&quot; are some words that can be confusing for non-english speakers. I had my fair share of difficulty with them, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:41:05-08:00","id":1032380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032041#post1032041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, some sleep should help.<br /> I try to say, what would character (with Status Merit not with Resource Merit) should do when shit hit the fan? He does not have his disposable money or another form of wealth (he does not have Resource merit) - he only have what he can afford by his Status. He will try automatically press by his authority? In common pace in dire situation most people try to buy off from this, because other methods much harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same thing anyone who doesn't have any liquid assets does when they need emergency funds - sell some of their stuff. He surely has Equipment he can sell for Cash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032041#post1032041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This topic popup with question: should character backup his status with money (and vise versa)? Most answers sound as &amp;quot;No, he does not&amp;quot; with foundation for this describer as &amp;quot;he has zero balance on end of month&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;he does not have disposable resources&amp;quot; which looks synonymous. Such answer implies that character have some income which steadiness not insured (who is it guaranteed?). And what will character do, if he loose his income (when he does not have Resource merit at all)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is a bit more complicated than that. A player doesn't have to &quot;back up&quot; their character's Status with Resources, because Resources represents income that is both consistent and disposable, and it is entirely possible for a character to have high standing in a well-paying job and still not have disposable income, if all of their income is going towards paying off recurring expenses. Heck, a player doesn't even <i>have to</i> &quot;back up&quot; their character's important CEO job with Status dots, because Status represents power within the organization, and it's entirely possible for a CEO to delegate all of his responsibilities to other employees and have no real power. But if the question is, &quot;<i>should</i> a player back up his character's stuff with Merits?&quot; then the answer is, &quot;it depends.&quot; It depends on the character's story and what mechanical advantages the player wants to get out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032041#post1032041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he is a &amp;quot;good&amp;quot; ST he does not use such cheap tricks. If he is &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; ST then he not just use such stunt but worsens situation by all means combining all similar factors (when presence of privilege is not guaranteed). But &amp;quot;realistic&amp;quot; ST not simple use but permits...</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, this depends on the group and what they want. Generally speaking though, an ST should work with the players to determine what they want out of the story, and introduce or not introduce complications accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:53:50-08:00","id":1032385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032362#post1032362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he just wanted to use &quot;must&quot; instead of &quot;should&quot;. &quot;May&quot;, &quot;Can&quot;, &quot;Should&quot; and &quot;Must&quot; are some words that can be confusing for non-english speakers. I had my fair share of difficulty with them, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the possible language barrier issue there, but the answer essentially remains the same between all of those words. The semantic nuances between them in English aren't really relevant to the specifics of the topic, they just influence the best way to phrase the response.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T17:07:24-08:00","id":1032393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032385#post1032385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the possible language barrier issue there, but the answer essentially remains the same between all of those words. The semantic nuances between them in English aren't really relevant to the specifics of the topic, they just influence the best way to phrase the response.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually find it relevant. In this case, &quot;should not&quot; would mean that you have to avoid linking them, while &quot;must not&quot; means that it is optional, instead of mandatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T17:31:25-08:00","id":1032404,"title":"","content":"A mind twister:<br /> You can have 5 Resources and literally 0 money. How? You might be a Rat King Of Garbage Ville, who has literally 0$ to their name, no income, and technically homeless. Resources 5 could just reflect his vast collection of *weird stuff* that can be found in his lair. So...you need an indian knife that killed a Pope? And GM rates it's Availability as 5?<br /> He found it one day when searching through garbage. <br /> <br /> (And to be clear, I don't want to be offensive. I just want to show a different approach to Resources that doesn't involve helicopters and millionaires)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T19:39:49-08:00","id":1032432,"title":"","content":"The Resource merit doesn't represent wither or not your character owns a million dollar Ferrari or has the ability to save up for one in the future, instead it represents wither or not your character has the means to buy a car on short notice, right now and in cash.<br /> It's an abstract system that is only meant to effect your character's available resources during a play session, not what he may gain during the long empty spaces in between.<br /> On a related note I seem to remember reading somewhere that you can temporarily boost your effective Resource dots by taking a condition that temporarily reduces them afterwards, representing your character having leveraged himself financially and the time it takes to climb out of the red.<br /> This wouldn't help a character with zero dots in Resources, if he wants that car he is going to have to steal it (or borrow it, exchange favors for it or use a different merit to achieve it).<br /> All of that in-between stuff is for the player and story teller to work out, outside of the rules. It just shouldn't be available any time the character discovers he needs something right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 01-15-2017, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T19:41:46-08:00","id":1032433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032404#post1032404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mind twister:<br /> You can have 5 Resources and literally 0 money. How? You might be a Rat King Of Garbage Ville, who has literally 0$ to their name, no income, and technically homeless. Resources 5 could just reflect his vast collection of *weird stuff* that can be found in his lair. So...you need an indian knife that killed a Pope? And GM rates it's Availability as 5?<br /> He found it one day when searching through garbage. <br /> <br /> (And to be clear, I don't want to be offensive. I just want to show a different approach to Resources that doesn't involve helicopters and millionaires)</div> </div> </div> </div>:/ I guess... I feel like that would work better as a different Merit though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T19:43:55-08:00","id":1032436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032432#post1032432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note I seem to remember reading somewhere that you can temporarily boost your effective Resource dots by taking a condition that temporarily reduces them afterwards, representing your character having leveraged himself financially and the time it takes to climb out of the red.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's ot a Condition, it's just part of the Merit's effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T23:42:11-08:00","id":1032514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have 5 Resources and literally 0 money. How? You might be a Rat King Of Garbage Ville, who has literally 0$ to their name, no income, and technically homeless. Resources 5 could just reflect his vast collection of *weird stuff* that can be found in his lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would avoid this use of Resources. Each gizmo may require its description. And it may put Storyteller in a difficult position, wondering whether to let you just have this thing or you should obtain it: on the one hand mechanically you can possess any kind of contraption, and on other hand (again) mechanically each thing is unique (and <b>may </b>have cost in EXP).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-16-2017, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T03:00:06-08:00","id":1032564,"title":"","content":"From the extremes of a millionare with Resources 0 to a humble worker with Resources 5 there is a space that I see it has to be negotiated between narrator and players, basically to make things coherent and avoid abuse.<br /> <br /> As Narrator I want to give the players what they want to play, I want them happy, but I want some reciprocity and flexibility from them to adapt their characters a bit for the sake of the story (and for the sake of the mental sanity of the narrator).<br /> <br /> So, if a player wants a Millionare but invest no merit point in Resources, I will have him invest merit points in things coherent with the social status he wants to have. I also will make him understand that I will not allow abuses, like telling me that his character has 5 Ferraris and then in game selling one and asking me to give him 3 cash equipment of 5 each one, or sell his mansion to rise to a Resources 3 merit for free. <br /> <br /> Narrative flavour, yes. Rules cheating, nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:37:43-08:00","id":1032760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032514#post1032514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would avoid this use of Resources. Each gizmo may require its description. And it may put Storyteller in a difficult position, wondering whether to let you just have this thing or you should obtain it: on the one hand mechanically you can possess any kind of contraption, and on other hand (again) mechanically each thing is unique (and <b>may </b>have cost in EXP).</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... No, equipment never costs experiences. It is acquired by its Availability, using either Resources or another Merit such as Status or Allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:13:17-08:00","id":1032816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err... No, equipment never costs experiences. It is acquired by its Availability, using either Resources or another Merit such as Status or Allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point not there. Even if any equipment never cost experiences i prefer not to give players unique items only for their pretty eyes (read only for Resources). I dislike idea that unique equipment can be purchased (even when their availability lesser then Resources). And here the whole concept of Resources is built on the unique objects. Unique item can not be just purchased: character should in first find where he can buy it (use Contacts or Allies). Then he should find the right approach to seller (Rat King himself quite interest concept for typical bargain). And I seriously doubt that, even agreeing to the deal, the Rat King will agree to sell his goods for money (or other <u>disposable</u> wealth).<br /> <br /> Update: and some merits can be <i>crafted </i>and have physical embodiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-16-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:24:15-08:00","id":1032875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032816#post1032816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point not there. Even if any equipment never cost experiences i prefer not to give players unique items only for their pretty eyes (read only for Resources). I dislike idea that unique equipment can be purchased (even when their availability lesser then Resources). And here the whole concept of Resources is built on the unique objects. Unique item can not be just purchased: character should in first find where he can buy it (use Contacts or Allies). Then he should find the right approach to seller (Rat King himself quite interest concept for typical bargain). And I seriously doubt that, even agreeing to the deal, the Rat King will agree to sell his goods for money (or other <u>disposable</u> wealth).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood what WHW was saying. The point wasn't about using Resources to acquire unique items, it was about allowing players to acquire equipment using Resources, representing something other than actual money. In this example, the character just has a bunch of stuff they've collected, so while mechanically they may be using their Resources Merit to acquire a piece of Equipment with Availability equal to or less than their Dots in Resources (let's say Automotive Equipment, from page 270 of Chronicles of Darkness), in the narrative they might just be finding in their collection of junk they've stockpiled over the years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1032816#post1032816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Update: and some merits can be <i>crafted </i>and have physical embodiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they can't. <i>Equipment</i> can be crafted, but <i>Merits</i> cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:52:36-08:00","id":1033000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">piece of Equipment with Availability equal to or less than their Dots in Resources</div> </div> </div> </div>And instead of Ferrari you acquire retro-car. Okey. Prices actually match. But yet here performance characteristics. What about them? If Merit <u>mechanically</u> alow you obtain items then character should be able to get the appropriate equipment.<br /> Not that I against it. However, it is a slippery slope.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they can't. <i>Equipment</i> can be crafted, but <i>Merits</i> cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, really! Even when you adapt you Lucky coin to any yes-no questioning Merit? Or even when you pickup cursed jewelry with Destiny on it?<br /> It's not CofD rule but literary trope which you can engine through Merits. PC definitely can craft a Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T23:57:54-08:00","id":1033191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1033000#post1033000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, really! Even when you adapt you Lucky coin to any yes-no questioning Merit? Or even when you pickup cursed jewelry with Destiny on it?<br /> It's not CofD rule but literary trope which you can engine through Merits. PC definitely can craft a Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a habit of confusing Mechanical terms and common terms.<br /> You cannot Craft (the CofD subsystem, not the common word) merits.<br /> <br /> You're also throwing in house rules and trying to have a discussion around them as if they're a de facto part of the setting. Destiny is a merit a person possesses, that says THEY have a Destiny. If the merit isn't specifically about an object (there are some that are), then making it about an object you possess is a houserule.<br /> <br /> You can't have honest conversations about the setting unless you're talking about it as-written.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting - if you create an Imbued Item, for example: you don't have to take the merit for it.<br /> So even using common terminology, you don't craft merits. At best, you can craft things that can also be represented at merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-17-2017, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:34:29-08:00","id":1033203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot Craft (the CofD subsystem, not the common word) merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>PC definitely can craft a Merit. Things just don't popup randomly. They appear for some reason. And when PC craft something (player just may ask imbue merit's quality to it) it's also may be reason.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're also throwing in house rules and trying to have a discussion around them as if they're a de facto part of the setting</div> </div> </div> </div>As i say it's not CofD rule (nor official nor homebrew). Mechanically it's change nothing. It's does not add dices or add some privilege for PC. It's the literary trope. It's add some flavor to merit. Some charmed items can return to their owners even after being stolen. Or they may be destroyed. In general, if you present them in such a way, they were made possible as getting and losing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> then making it about an object you possess is a houserule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okey if you see it so. But<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the merit isn't specifically about an object (there are some that are)</div> </div> </div> </div>PC definitely can craft such a Merit.<br /> Alternate Identity (2nd and 3rd dots) can be obtained through PCs craft and activity (without third party).<br /> As was said Resources can presents as objects and they definitely can be crafted. Say can i draw a picture with estimate price on it adequate for 2nd-3rd dot in Resources, can't i?<br /> Safe Place. Striking Looks (not for themselves but for character in party). Clairvoyance.<br /> It's not about rules, it's about causes. Nothing can appear from nowhere. And crafting it (and using craft rules for this) - one of a way of obtaining it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-17-2017, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:40:03-08:00","id":1033205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1033203#post1033203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PC definitely can craft a Merit. Things just don't popup randomly. They appear for some reason. And when PC craft something (player just may ask imbue merit's quality to it) it's also may be reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't understand (or even see) the distinction between 'crafting a merit' and 'crafting the narrative justification for purchasing a merit'.<br /> I'll say it one last time - you don't craft merits. You pay experience for them.<br /> <br /> Reference the crafting rules for an example:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Organizations built as equipment usually disband after one game session unless the player purchases them as Merits afterward </div> </div> </div>You're inserting all of your setting assumptions and house rules into the discussion and complicating it for everyone.<br /> That kind of makes discussion impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1033203#post1033203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As was said Resources can presents as objects.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Not without house rules.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Effect: </b>This Merit reflects your character\u2019s disposable in-come. </div> </div> </div>The place to have a discussion about all of your house rules for Status/Resources/Crafting is not a thread someone else started to understand how they work as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-17-2017, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:02:57-08:00","id":1033239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll say it one last time</div> </div> </div> </div>do You feel offended?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I know that i can receive another admonition for this. I just can not suppress my irritation</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't understand (or even see) the distinction between 'crafting a merit' and 'crafting the narrative justification for purchasing a merit'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Player may buy or not, create as temporal and ransom afterwards, destroy in process what was ransomed before. Fixation - entirely on the player's conscience.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Not without house rules.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Who says so? And don't take things out of context.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofD_core_book.p.53_Resources</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dot rating determines the relative amount of disposable funding the character has available, depending on your particular chronicle\u2019s setting</div> </div> </div> </div>It's may be gold, bottle caps, gun shells - whatever you can freely exchange as currency. And for pure barter almost everything.<br /> This situation has been repeatedly described in this thread.<br /> <br /> And sorry for my inability to bring you my point of view.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030128#post1030128\">This is incredibly untrue</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Point there you does not have safe income without Resource dots. And still with Resource dots you does not have safe income. But if you have income at all (as narrative element) you always can produce some cash.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030189#post1030189\">Source? Or is this your house rule to make the rules align better with your worldview/gameplay style?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>How about justification for transferring dots from one merit to another. It's not about why you can do it (what/who allow it). It's about why you can't do it. You miss whole point there that's is no rule except ST decision what can ban such action.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030611#post1030611\">This. We're having a conversation about Resources, which is explicitly <i>extra</i> disposable <i>income</i>, not 'having money'.<br /> Instead of making bizarre houserules, use Cash Equipment (aka 'having money') for what it was made for, and Resources for what it was made for, maybe?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Player may just receive Cash equipment or decide to ransom whole Resource merit (through Sanctity of Merits).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1030659#post1030659\">That means it's 'spent' (mechanically) in the same way the merit is, not that it fills the same narrative role. Resources remain disposable income. Cash is cash.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Or character may receive each month Cash equipment for causes of having Resource merit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The place to have a discussion about all of your house rules for Status/Resources/Crafting is not a thread someone else started to understand how they work as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for you are missing point. The whole &quot;5 cents&quot; where was you not have safe and steady income without Resource dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-17-2017, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:56:42-08:00","id":1033468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1033239#post1033239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do You feel offended?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I know that i can receive another admonition for this. I just can not suppress my irritation</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Yes, you will. And since you've been warned about exactly this before, it's going to be a one week suspension this time. Don't do it again, or it'll be a longer suspension next time, and may lead to a permanent ban if it becomes a pattern.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T00:19:43-08:00","id":1033906,"title":"","content":"I want to make sure I have all of this right, based on what I've read here:<br /> -Characters can craft or acquire Equipment, and said Equipment provides its Equipment Bonus.<br /> -Merits can be involved in buying or finding Equipment when appropriate. Resources is the go-to in most cases, although some Social Merits may be used in some cases as per Availability and Procurement (CofD 100). <br /> -Generally, Characters can't create/purchase/find Equipment that confers a Merit, either permanently or temporarily. Any exceptions have to be explicit, such as using a Disguise to emulate one dot of a Social Merit.<br /> -Merits with physical representations (such as Object Fetishism) generally don't require said physical representation to be paid for/found/etc. The Storyteller may say that the item should be crafted/bought/found to justify purchasing the Merit, but that's something that the rules don't require and that should be discussed within the group.<br /> -Objects that are physically representative of a Merit are not Equipment; that is to say, they generally don't carry their own Equipment Bonus separate from the Merit. Any exceptions would have to be discussed in-group.<br /> -Trading Dots from one Merit to another (e.g. Sacrificing Status to gain Resources or vice versa) is technically possible under Sanctity of Merits, but it requires ST acceptance. Sanctity of Merits is generally there to allow characters to change appropriately given proper circumstances, not to turn your Merit Dots into a floating pool you can re-allocate willy nilly. (Easy Come, Easy Go [HL 81] being the only in-rule exception I've found so far.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T01:30:29-08:00","id":1033917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1033906#post1033906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to make sure I have all of this right, based on what I've read here:<br /> -Characters can craft or acquire Equipment, and said Equipment provides its Equipment Bonus.<br /> -Merits can be involved in buying or finding Equipment when appropriate. Resources is the go-to in most cases, although some Social Merits may be used in some cases as per Availability and Procurement (CofD 100).<br /> -Generally, Characters can't create/purchase/find Equipment that confers a Merit, either permanently or temporarily. Any exceptions have to be explicit, such as using a Disguise to emulate one dot of a Social Merit.<br /> -Merits with physical representations (such as Object Fetishism) generally don't require said physical representation to be paid for/found/etc. The Storyteller may say that the item should be crafted/bought/found to justify purchasing the Merit, but that's something that the rules don't require and that should be discussed within the group.<br /> -Objects that are physically representative of a Merit are not Equipment; that is to say, they generally don't carry their own Equipment Bonus separate from the Merit. Any exceptions would have to be discussed in-group.<br /> -Trading Dots from one Merit to another (e.g. Sacrificing Status to gain Resources or vice versa) is technically possible under Sanctity of Merits, but it requires ST acceptance. Sanctity of Merits is generally there to allow characters to change appropriately given proper circumstances, not to turn your Merit Dots into a floating pool you can re-allocate willy nilly. (Easy Come, Easy Go [HL 81] being the only in-rule exception I've found so far.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything you've listed looks correct to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}